{"classified_as":[{"_id":"http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300033799","label":"oil paintings (visual works)","type":"Type"},{"_id":"http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300033618","label":"paintings (visual works)","type":"Type"},{"_label":"Collection Item","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404024","type":"Type"}],"id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/object/8612","identified_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"catalogue raisonnée number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026061"}],"content":"540","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"repository number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404621"}],"content":"8612","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"non-preferred identifiers","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300264273"}],"content":"540, Catalogue Raisonné","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"non-preferred identifiers","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300264273"}],"content":{"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne":{"titles":[{"notes":"Source of title: Whitney Archive.","title":"The Seashell and Old Shingle","type":"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"},{"notes":"Source of title: Whitney Archive. (Title used by MFA Boston.)","title":"Shell and Old Shingle No. I","type":"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"},{"notes":"Source of title: Downtown Gallery Archive.","title":"Shell and Old Shingle – No. I","type":"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"},{"notes":"Source of title: Downtown Gallery Archive.","title":"Shell and Old Shingle","type":"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"}],"type":"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"},"title-1999-catalogue-raisonne":{"titles":[{"notes":"Source of title: backing inscription, Abiquiú Notebooks.","title":"Shell and Old Shingle I/Shell and Old Shingle No. I","type":"title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"}],"type":"title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"}},"type":"Name"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"preferred term","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670"}],"content":"Shell and Old Shingle I/Shell and Old Shingle No. I","type":"Name"}],"produced_by":{"carried_out_by":[{"_label":"Georgia O'Keeffe","id":"actor/2","type":"Actor"}],"timespan":{"type":"TimeSpan"},"type":"Production"},"referred_to_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Artist(s)","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_artist"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"credit line","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026687"}],"content":"Alfred Stieglitz Collection—Bequest of Georgia O'Keeffe ","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Materials description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/materials_description"}],"content":"Oil on canvas","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Title and Date","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_title_date"}],"content":"Shell and Old Shingle I/Shell and Old Shingle No. I, 1926","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Holding Institution","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_instituion"}],"content":"Museum of Fine Arts (MFA Boston)","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Complete","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_complete"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe. Shell and Old Shingle I/Shell and Old Shingle No. I, 1926. Oil on canvas, 9 x 7 inches. Museum of Fine Arts (MFA Boston). Alfred Stieglitz Collection—Bequest of Georgia O'Keeffe . © Museum of Fine Arts (MFA Boston)","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Copyright","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_copyright"}],"content":"© Museum of Fine Arts (MFA Boston)","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Measurement Description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/measurement_description"}],"content":"9 x 7 inches","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Medium and Dimensions","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_medium_dims"}],"content":"Oil on canvas, 9 x 7 inches","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"provenance_narrative","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/provenance_narrative"}],"content":"1987, bequest of the artist to the MFA. (Accession Date: October 28, 1987) \n(Source: MFA Boston, 2025)","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"description statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"}],"content":"The smooth, white form of an open seashell peeks into the canvas from below. Behind the shell is the rough, gray surface of a shingle placed on its side. A soft green leaf extends into the canvas from the upper right edge.","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"cr_remarks_1999","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/cr_remarks_1999"}],"content":["Double entries Downtown Gallery Archive. \"No. I\" in first title written in by O'Keeffe in graphite in Abiquiú Notebooks. Whitney Archive indicates, \"Exam. at Amer. Place, March 1946. . No signature [notes backing inscription]. Grey shingle with white shell at base. Two green leaves upper right, one partly shown.\" Abiquiú Notebooks indicates, \"Back: On stretcher by A.S., 'Georgia O'Keeffe – 1926 – Shell and Old Shingle No. I.\" [inscription is not on this work but on stretcher of cat. entry 545]. Part of series renumbered by O'Keeffe and DB in 1970. O'Keeffe wrote: \"We were shingling the barn and the old shingles, taken off, were free to fly around. Absentmindedly I picked up a loose one and carried it into the house and up to the table in my room. On the table was a white clam shell brought from Maine in the spring. I had been painting it and it still lay there. The white shape of the shell and the grey shape of the weathered shingle were beautiful against the pale grey leaf on the faintly pink-lined pattern of the wallpaper. Adding the shingle got me painting again. After the first realistic paintings I painted just a piece of the shingle and a piece of the shell. To a couple were added two quite large green leaves that were in a glass on the table. Finally I went back to the shingle and shell —large again— the shingle just a dark shape that floated off the top of the painting, the shell just a simple white shape under it. They fascinated me so that I forgot what they were except that they were shapes together — singing shapes\" (*Georgia O'Keeffe* [1976], unpaginated, text accompanying entry 51). (Source: Lynes, 1999)"],"type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[{"digitally_shown_by":[{"access_point":[{"id":"https://iiif.okeeffemuseum.org/image/iiif/2/792250/full/full/0/default.jpg","type":"DigitalObject"}],"classified_as":[{"_label":"Digital Image","id":"http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300215302","type":"Type"}],"digitally_available_via":[{"access_point":[{"id":"https://iiif.okeeffemuseum.org/image/iiif/2/792250"}],"conforms_to":[{"id":"http://iiif.io/api/image","type":"InformationObject"}],"format":"application/ld+json;profile='http://iiif.io/api/image/2/context.json'","type":"DigitalService"}],"type":"DigitalObject"}],"type":"VisualItem"}],"type":"HumanMadeObject"}